        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "undaa",
          "x": 2184,
          "y": 148,
          "name": "unifiedAddProjectNote",
          "width": 360,
          "height": 420,
          "content": "One form, Source as a field\n\nThe two source tiles were a mode switch pretending to be content. Making Source the first field removes the switch and lets both branches share Project manager, Visibility and Default billable — which is the whole point of the change.\n\nWHAT THIS COSTS\n\nProject manager: nothing. /projects/new is admin-only and createAssignment requires admin, so the form can import and then assign, exactly as the manual path already does.\n\nVisibility and Default billable: the import endpoint must accept them. Today importBoard inserts only {workspaceId, name, color}, so imported projects silently take the column defaults private and billable=true. Showing the fields without that change would be a lie.\n\nAdd them per project in importGitHubProjectsSchema (it is .strict() and takes up to 25), not top-level, so a future multi-select import can still differ per project.\n\nSEPARATE, NOT FIXED HERE\n\ncreateProject assigns the creator when the caller is a PM; importBoard does not. No PM reaches this page today, so nothing breaks, but the two paths disagree."
        },
