        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "hQeaa",
          "x": 824,
          "y": 1432,
          "name": "githubImportFormNote",
          "width": 340,
          "height": 340,
          "content": "GitHub import as a form\n\nTwo fields, then a verdict. Organization scopes the search; project chooses; the block below states exactly what pressing Add project will create.\n\nEverything the old cards crammed into one tile is now a labelled row, and the sentence under the rows names the consequence rather than the fact — why a repository is linked or why none is.\n\nProject name, Source and Linked repository are derived, never typed: the import endpoint accepts none of them.\n\nAlready-added projects stay listed and greyed, so an admin sees the project exists rather than wondering why it is missing."
        },
