        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "T95EjT",
          "x": 1874,
          "y": 2439,
          "name": "mobileRedesignNote",
          "width": 340,
          "height": 420,
          "content": "Mobile redesign — saved bar + Group by\n\nSAVED REPORTS BAR (mobile branch only; desktop untouched)\n• Row 1: 40px pill strip, ACTIVE preset emphasized (accent-tint + 1.5px brand border + bookmark); a decorative amber dot sits on the active pill when dirty. ⋯ manage + ＋ new fused into one app-bg capsule (two 40px thumb zones, hairline between).\n• Row 2 is CONTEXTUAL — kills the old dead disabled Save:\n  – Clean + loaded → “✓ Saved · {name}” + Save as… (outlined). No Save button.\n  – Dirty + loaded → “● Unsaved changes” + Save (accent-tint) + Save as…\n  – Dirty + unsaved → single promoted “Save as new…”.\n• All testids preserved (strip/tabs/manage/new/save/save-as/dirty).\n\nGROUP BY BUILDER (new mobile branch; desktop chips untouched)\n• Vertical numbered pipeline (1→2→3) — replaces the horizontal draggable chips that are unusable on touch.\n• Each step card: number badge + dimension + “Top level / within {prev}” drill-down caption + ALWAYS-VISIBLE 40px up/down stepper (fixes the hover-gated controls) + remove.\n• “+ Add level” is a real 48px full-width dashed field — fixes the broken class-merge via a NEW exported PT token (giTiempoAddLevelSelectMobilePt), never mutating the shared one.\n• Reuses every existing reorder/add/remove handler + full keyboard grab model + all testids; adds ↑/↓ keys alongside ←/→.\n\nNext: implement both behind useIsMobileViewport, keep desktop byte-identical, keep specs green."
        },
