                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hDnaS",
                  "fill": "$color-text-dark",
                  "content": "Privacy Policy",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                  "fontSize": 50,
                  "fontWeight": "700",
                  "letterSpacing": -2.2
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "SeFt5",
                  "fill": "$color-text-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "How GITiempo handles personal data in the service and Chrome extension.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "M4n03O",
                  "fill": "$color-text-muted",
                  "content": "Last updated: 18 August 2026",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "Ky1WA",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 1,
                  "fill": "$color-divider"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JFUo8",
                  "fill": "$color-text-dark",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "1. Controller and contact\n\n2. Information we process\nWhen you start a timer from a supported GitHub issue, the extension sends the repository name, issue number, issue title and canonical direct issue URL to GiTiempo. It reads the visible issue context to prepare this request; it does not monitor your general browsing history.\n\n3. How we use information\nFor projects connected through a workspace GitHub App installation, GiTiempo verifies access and retrieves issue information from GitHub. For external-reference tracking, it records the issue context you supply without retrieving it through the GitHub API or verifying your GitHub access.\n\n4. Sharing and authentication services\nA workspace can reuse the same project and issue task for multiple members. Tracking alone lets you see your own time entries and the projects and exact tasks containing them, including a running entry. It does not expose other members’ time or tasks. Workspace administrators and people with separately granted project access can see records according to their permissions.\n\n5. Retention and security\nRemoving or moving your last time entry removes the access derived from that entry. It does not automatically delete the shared project, task or other members’ records. Separate project access may remain.\n\n6. Your choices and rights\nSigning out or uninstalling the extension does not delete server records or stop a running timer.\n\n7. Changes to this policy\n\n8. Optional homepage analytics",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
